    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430-a2">

                <pb facs="0472" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg438"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure in No. 485.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Zeleno<hi
                                rendition="#superscript">i</hi> to Mr. Aarons.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Russian Imperial Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20/November 1,
                                1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 488.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter I have the
                    honor to inform you that everyone who left Russia before his enlistment in the
                    army on his return to that country must serve his term, which is five years.
                    Before speaking of a permit I found it necessary to announce you this matter. If
                    Mr. Harry Marks is willing to serve his country five years as a soldier we can
                    consider his case.</p>
                <p>Believe me, sir, yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Zelenoi</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Russian
                    Legation.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
